Task 3: Testing Access Controls with Different Users
Subtask 3.1: Test Administrative Access
Test admin user access:
# Test HBAC rules for admin user
ipa hbactest --user=testadmin --host=idm-server.example.com --service=sshd
ipa hbactest --user=testadmin --host=client1.example.com --service=sudo

# Expected result: Access should be allowed for both tests
Verify admin can access all systems:
# From a separate terminal, test actual SSH access
# Open new terminal and try to SSH as testadmin
ssh testadmin@idm-server.example.com
# Enter password when prompted

# Test sudo access
sudo whoami
# Should return 'root'

# Exit and test client access
exit
ssh testadmin@client1.example.com
sudo whoami
exit
Subtask 3.2: Test Regular User Access
Test regular user restrictions:
# Test HBAC rules for regular user
ipa hbactest --user=testuser1 --host=idm-server.example.com --service=sshd
# Expected result: Access DENIED

ipa hbactest --user=testuser1 --host=client1.example.com --service=sshd
# Expected result: Access ALLOWED

ipa hbactest --user=testuser1 --host=client1.example.com --service=sudo
# Expected result: Access DENIED
Verify actual access behavior:
# Test actual SSH access for regular user
# From separate terminal:
ssh testuser1@idm-server.example.com
# Should be denied or fail

ssh testuser1@client1.example.com
# Should succeed

# Once logged in as testuser1:
sudo whoami
# Should fail with permission denied
exit
Subtask 3.3: Test Developer Access
Test developer-specific rules:
# Test HBAC rules for developer
ipa hbactest --user=developer1 --host=client1.example.com --service=sshd
# Expected result: Access ALLOWED

ipa hbactest --user=developer1 --host=client1.example.com --service=sudo
# Expected result: Access ALLOWED

ipa hbactest --user=developer1 --host=client2.example.com --service=sshd
# Expected result: Access DENIED (not in developer_access rule)
Verify developer sudo access:
# Test actual access
ssh developer1@client1.example.com
# Should succeed

# Test sudo access
sudo whoami
# Should return 'root'

# Test access to restricted host
exit
ssh developer1@client2.example.com
# Should be denied
Subtask 3.4: Comprehensive Access Testing
Create a test matrix:
# Create a script to test multiple scenarios
cat > /tmp/test_access.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash

echo "=== HBAC Access Test Matrix ==="
echo

# Test scenarios
scenarios=(
    "testadmin idm-server.example.com sshd"
    "testadmin client1.example.com sudo"
    "testuser1 idm-server.example.com sshd"
    "testuser1 client1.example.com sshd"
    "testuser1 client1.example.com sudo"
    "developer1 client1.example.com sshd"
    "developer1 client1.example.com sudo"
    "developer1 client2.example.com sshd"
)

for scenario in "${scenarios[@]}"; do
    read -r user host service <<< "$scenario"
    echo -n "Testing $user -> $host ($service): "
    result=$(ipa hbactest --user="$user" --host="$host" --service="$service" 2>/dev/null | grep -o "Access.*")
    echo "$result"
done
EOF

chmod +x /tmp/test_access.sh
/tmp/test_access.sh
