Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Access Denied Despite Correct Rules
Problem: User cannot access system even though HBAC test shows access should be allowed.

Solution:

# Check SSSD cache and refresh
systemctl restart sssd

# Clear SSSD cache
sss_cache -E

# Verify client is properly enrolled
ipa-client-install --unattended --force-join

# Check SSSD logs
tail -f /var/log/sssd/sssd_domain.log
Issue 2: HBAC Test Shows Different Results Than Expected
Problem: ipa hbactest results don't match the configured rules.

Solution:

# Verify rule is enabled
ipa hbacrule-show rulename --all

# Check for conflicting rules
ipa hbacrule-find --enabled=true

# Verify user group membership
ipa user-show username --all

# Check host enrollment
ipa host-show hostname.domain.com
Issue 3: Sudo Access Not Working Despite HBAC Rules
Problem: User can SSH but sudo doesn't work even with proper HBAC rules.

Solution:

# Check sudo rules separately
ipa sudorule-find --users=username

# Verify sudo service in HBAC rule
ipa hbacrule-show rulename --all

# Check sudoers configuration on client
sudo visudo -c

# Restart SSSD on client
systemctl restart sssd
